            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Indira"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My husband and I grew blue pumpkins in our garden this year and I have been looking for pumpkin recipes ever since. I made this dish for 2 Thanksgiving dinners that I attended and everyone LOVED it so much. Thank you for posting such an easy and delicious recipe!!!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ekai"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Turned out great. I cut it into 1 inch pieces and added bread crumbs to the mixture (in a bowl, mix flour, bread crumbs, salt &amp; pepper, then make sure pumpkin is slightly wet, toss in a handful, shake to coat, then pan fry in butter). Would make again!",
            "datePublished": "2019-01-16T02:07:50.257Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Annie-bird"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I prepared this dish with french fried cut pumpkin. I salted and peppered it and coated it in flour and then I fried it in olive oil. Yum! It tasted like fried potatoes plus a little sweetness. I will definitely make this again!",
            "datePublished": "2011-07-14T19:52:32.717Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "FILOMALI"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is really yummy. My kids don't like it but my husband and I ate the whole thing. I use olive oil instead of butter, and I added sweet paprika and garlic powder too. Similar to sweet potato fries. I left the pieces in the ziploc bag while doing other things and it started to get a little watery, but I proceeded to cook the pieces and they turned out fine. Will definitely make again. Thanks!",
            "datePublished": "2010-10-22T21:37:42.143Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "L'Heure Bleue"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yum! I was gifted a small pumpkin and hated to throw it away but we have too many sweets in the house. Made it last night and the only thing I changed was I made the chunks small and used half butter, half canola oil. My mom and adult daughter are both picky eaters, as am I, but it was so good we each had seconds. Crunchy and buttery, you can't go wrong with that!",
            "datePublished": "2015-12-20T09:10:19.790Z"
          },
          {
